xt":"எதிர்ந்தோர்க்கு","lemma":"etirntōr","gloss":"those who approached"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed to those who approached"},{"surface":"அங்கை","parts":[{"text":"அங்கை","lemma":"aṅkai","gloss":"palm of the hand"}],"gloss":"palm of the hand"},{"surface":"நண்மையன்","parts":[{"text":"நண்மையன்","lemma":"naṇmaiyaṉ","gloss":"one who is close"}],"gloss":"one who is close"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வல்வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வல்","lemma":"val","gloss":"strong"},{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"strong-speared"},{"surface":"கந்தன்","parts":[{"text":"கந்தன்","lemma":"kantaṉ","gloss":"Kandan"}],"gloss":"Kandan"},{"surface":"நல்லிசை","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"nal","gloss":"good"},{"text":"இசை","lemma":"icai","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"good fame"},{"surface":"அல்ல","parts":[{"text":"அல்ல","lemma":"alla","gloss":"not other than"}],"gloss":"not other than"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"…","parts":[{"text":"…","lemma":"…","gloss":"…"}],"gloss":"…"},{"surface":"தார்","parts":[{"text":"தார்","lemma":"tār","gloss":"garland"}],"gloss":"garland"},{"surface":"பிள்ளை","parts":[{"text":"பிள்ளை","lemma":"piḷḷai","gloss":"child"}],"gloss":"child"},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"சிறாஅர்","parts":[{"text":"சிறாஅர்","lemma":"ciṟāar","gloss":"children"}],"gloss":"children"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அன்னன்","parts":[{"text":"அன்னன்","lemma":"annaṉ","gloss":"such a person"}],"gloss":"such a person"},{"surface":"ஆகன்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகன்","lemma":"ākaṉ","gloss":"being"}],"gloss":"being"},{"surface":"மாறே","parts":[{"text":"மாறே","lemma":"māṟē","gloss":"because"}],"gloss":"because"},{"surface":"இந்நிலம்","parts":[{"text":"இந்நிலம்","lemma":"innilam","gloss":"this land"}],"gloss":"this land"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இலம்படு","parts":[{"text":"இலம்","lemma":"ilam","gloss":"poverty"},{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"occurring"}],"gloss":"poverty-stricken"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"time"},{"surface":"ஆயினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயினும்","lemma":"āyiṉum","gloss":"even if"}],"gloss":"even if"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புலம்பல்போ","parts":[{"text":"புலம்பல்போ","lemma":"புலம்பல்போ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யின்று","parts":[{"text":"யின்று","lemma":"யின்று","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பூத்தஎன்","parts":[{"text":"பூத்தஎன்","lemma":"பூத்தஎன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கடும்பே","parts":[{"text":"கடும்பே","lemma":"கடும்பே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Wearing pearls from the southern ocean / rubbing sandalwood from the northern hills / ... army like the ocean / with sweet-sounding victorious triumph / the strong warrior of the Southerners / the water poured on the heights spreads to the ocean and becomes pearls / the fragrant-petaled wild jasmine and kūtalam flowers droop / ... / the lord of Nāñcil hill with sweet-pulped jackfruit trees / to those who oppose him with hostility, he is far away and unthinking / to those who approach him with friendship, he is close like the palm of one's hand / Kandan of the strong spear, whose good fame is not other than / ... children with garlands / because he is such a person, in this land / even if it is a time of poverty / lamentation has gone, and my family has blossomed.","translation":"Wearing pearls from the southern ocean, and rubbing fragrant sandalwood from the northern hills, he commands an army vast as the sea. He is the strong warrior of the southern kings, winning sweet-sounding, glorious victories. The rain that pours on his high peaks flows down to the ocean to become pearls. On his slopes, fragrant wild jasmine and kūtalam flowers droop with moisture. He is the lord of Nāñcil hill, rich with sweet-pulped jackfruit trees. To those who oppose him with hostility, he is distant and unreachable; but to those who approach him in friendship, he is as close and welcoming as the palm of one's hand. Because Kandan of the strong spear, whose great fame is celebrated even by young children, is such a generous lord, even when poverty strikes this land, all lamentation has vanished from my family, and we have blossomed in prosperity.","modern":"தெற்குக் கடலின் முத்துக்களை அணிந்து, வடக்கிலுள்ள மலையின் சந்தனத்தைத் தேய்த்து, கடல் போன்ற படையைக் கொண்டு, இனிய இசையோடு கூடிய வெற்றிகளைப் பெறும் தென்னவர் (பாண்டியர்) வழிவந்த வலிமைமிக்க வீரன் அவன். மலையின் மேல் பெய்த நீர் கடலில் பரவி முத்தாக மாறுகிறது. நறுமணமுள்ள இதழ்களைக் கொண்ட காட்டு மல்லிகையும் கூதளம் பூக்களும் நனையும்படி, இனிமையான சுளைகளைக் கொண்ட பலா மரங்கள் நிறைந்த நாஞ்சில் மலையின் தலைவன் அவன். பகைமையோடு எதிர்ப்பவர்களுக்கு அவன் நினைத்துப் பார்க்க முடியாத தொலைவில் இருப்பவன்; நட்போடு அணுகுபவர்களுக்குத் தன் உள்ளங்கை போல மிக நெருக்கமானவன். வலிமையான வேலைக் கொண்ட கந்தனின் நல்ல புகழைப் பிள்ளைகளும் பாடுகின்றனர். அவன் அப்படிப்பட்டவனாக இருப்பதால், இந்நிலத்தில் வறுமைக்காலம் வந்தாலும், என் சுற்றத்தாரின் துன்பம் நீங்கி, அவர்கள் மகிழ்ச்சியோடு மலர்ந்து வாழ்கிறார்கள்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by a bard (pāṇar) praising Kandan, the chieftain of Nāñcil hill. The bard describes Kandan's dual nature: he is fiercely distant and unyielding to his enemies, yet incredibly close, warm, and generous to his friends and supplicants, like the very palm of one's hand. The rich landscape of Nāñcil hill, with its sweet jackfruit trees and abundant rain that washes down to the ocean to form pearls, mirrors the boundless generosity of its lord. Even when the rest of the land suffers from poverty, the bard's family is saved from distress and flourishes because of Kandan's patronage. Key words like 'cēymaiyaṉ' (one who is far) and 'naṇmaiyaṉ' (one who is close) beautifully contrast his attitude towards foes and friends.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}